# Production-only build vars for the platform (7aba.app).
#
# Committed on purpose. These are public analytics identifiers — they are
# emitted into the page HTML for every visitor, so they are not secrets and
# hiding them buys nothing. What it does buy: analytics work no matter who
# runs the build (CI, or a local `pnpm build` before `wrangler pages deploy`),
# instead of depending on one workflow file's env block.
#
# VITE_-prefixed values are inlined by Vite at build time. Setting them as
# Cloudflare Pages secrets would have no effect — nothing reads them at runtime.
# Both are also gated on NODE_ENV=production in src/utils/analytics/*, so dev
# and preview builds stay out of the reporting.

VITE_GOOGLE_ANALYTICS=G-YH3BLXWH1L
VITE_MICROSOFT_CLARITY_ID=xy3nad7qp7
